<h2 id="1-workshop-introduction">1. Workshop Introduction</h2>
<p>The Workshop on Secure Edge Intelligence and System Vulnerability Defense (SEIVD) focuses on the security challenges brought by edge computing, artificial intelligence, and intelligent system applications.
This workshop provides an academic communication platform for researchers and students to share original research, preliminary results, and engineering practices in edge security, vulnerability mining, and intelligent defense.</p>

<h2 id="2-topics-of-interest">2. Topics of Interest</h2>
<p>Topics include but are not limited to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Edge computing security and privacy protection</li>
  <li>Vulnerability detection and analysis of intelligent systems</li>
  <li>AI-driven attack detection and defense mechanism</li>
  <li>Lightweight security algorithm for edge devices</li>
  <li>IoT system security and data security</li>
  <li>Intrusion detection and threat intelligence</li>
  <li>Secure federated learning and privacy computing</li>
  <li>System security reinforcement and trusted execution</li>
</ul>

